{"kind":"assert","text":"EK-1 + ES-1 joint draft under 25f241cc (unapplied, uncompiled), with the export list before apply.\n\nExports from derive: one function and no types.\n- `judgeExploreGrant` (grant.ts:396). Its only caller outside derive is packages/mcp/src/inventory.ts:125.\n- `ExploreGrantStanding`, `ExploreGrantAsked` and `ExploreGrant` are written inline as Pick/Omit forms. `ExploreGrant` is plain `Omit\u003cGrant,\"fresh\"\u003e`.\n- No caller outside derive names `ExploreGrantJudgment` or `BodyJudgeContext`, so neither is exported. Derive tests take the types from `Parameters` and `ReturnType`.\n- The `revoked` widening stays. The grant canonical-bytes pin is in forms-grant.test.ts.\n\nSession-ending refusals, from source: one reason, `refused` with `unauthorized`. All seven `Unheld` failures in `judgeGrant` (grant.ts:257) give an empty grant list (authority.ts:336), which core.ts:683 answers as `unauthorized`. `authority-unavailable` answers `unavailable` and ends nothing. client/test/session.test.ts pins the set.\n\nMember kind: no membership rule binds a role to a kind. `invite-member` (membership.ts:359-379) takes any role with kind `person`, and only `add-member` binds one (:464-465). So the inventory leaves `kind` absent. MCP loses one thing: `#keepsOriginals` (service.ts:921) can no longer exclude agent or checker servers. A test pins both membership rows.\n\nChanged expectations so far: 8 lines in clone.test.ts, session-cache.test.ts, story.scope.test.ts and mcp/reads.test.ts. All are URL-matcher or fixture-routing edits, and no assertion changes its claim. The ES-1 inventory test is rewritten. The gate finds the rest, and END will list them.\n\nThree choices for you:\n1. The ES-1 draft always sent `?standing=1`. The application gateway (client/src/application-gateway.ts:56, sandbox worker.ts:48) refuses any query on POST sessions, and the Counter screen runs behind it. The joint draft asks only when the caller passes `standing: true`; only MCP and the CLI do. The other way is to let the gateway pass `standing`, with a test and a sandbox row in entry-points.md. Which one?\n2. Member kind can come from the membership summary's member item, which the inventory already reads. Do I read it from there, or leave it absent?\n3. The derive change alters sealed sources (judge.ts, sessions.ts, object.ts, worker.ts in security-entry-points.test.mjs). I re-seal them at apply with the owner's seal tool. Yes?","body":{"draft":"/private/tmp/artroom-ek1-es1-joint-20261116 joint.patch 135403 B sha256 6511e3b8deb42f11f63937a3b695588f3204bd02c6c1f3359965312eaf9ef6f3, 27 files","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}